---
/**
 * The questions people ask before paying, shown below the price on both the
 * pricing and Pro pages.
 */

/*
 * PLACEHOLDER. Not a figure anybody has stood behind yet, so it must be set
 * from beta usage before the price goes live.
 */
const readAllowance = '2,000';

const questions = [
  {
    question: 'Is the free version limited in any way?',
    answer:
      'No. It is the whole app, free and open source, with no time limit and nothing held back. Pro adds publishing, sync, and AI on top of it.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Do I need an account?',
    answer:
      'Only for Pro, which needs one to sync and publish. The free version asks for nothing and works without an internet connection.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens if I stop paying?',
    answer:
      'Your entries stay where they are, as plain files on your computer, and the app keeps working. Sync and any published pages carry on for 14 days after a subscription ends, then stop.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens to the copy on your servers?',
    answer:
      'It is deleted within 30 days of a subscription ending. You can also delete it yourself at any point, from the app, without ending your subscription.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What if I lose my encryption key?',
    answer:
      'Nothing we can do brings it back, since we never hold it. You are given a recovery key when you turn sync on, so keep it somewhere safe. Even without either, your entries are still plain files on your computer.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How many devices can I sync?',
    answer: 'As many as you use. There is no device limit on a subscription.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Are the AI features capped?',
    answer: `Only reading, since taking in images, documents, and web pages is the costly part. Those count against ${readAllowance} reads a month, however they arrive, whether you dropped one in yourself, pasted a link, a watched folder picked it up, or an automation did. Everything else is unlimited: designs, databases, automations, questions, and the everyday filling in of properties.`,
  },
  {
    question: 'What is a read?',
    answer:
      'One image, or around a thousand words of text, which is roughly two pages of a document. It counts the same wherever the words come from, so there is nothing to weigh up between attaching a document and pasting it in.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does a long document use up my whole month?',
    answer:
      'No. Filing something reads only as much as it needs, usually the first page or two, so a long PDF costs a couple of reads rather than hundreds. Asking for a summary of the whole thing reads the whole thing, and costs accordingly.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What if I need more than that?',
    answer:
      'Connect your own API key, or point MindDrop at a model running on your own machine, and the AI features run through it with no limit and no extra charge. Top-ups are there if you would rather we handled it.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is tax included in the price?',
    answer:
      'Yes. Prices are in USD, with VAT and sales tax already included, so the amount you see is the amount you pay.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I get a refund?',
    answer:
      'Yes. Ask within 14 days of paying and you get the whole amount back.',
  },
];
---

<section class="page faq">
  <h2 class="faq-title">FAQ</h2>

  <div class="faq-list">
    {
      questions.map((question) => (
        <article class="faq-question">
          <h3 class="faq-question-title">{question.question}</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">{question.answer}</p>
        </article>
      ))
    }
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-9);
  }

  .faq-title {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-7);
  }

  .faq-question-title {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .faq-list {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
